Manual patches: best is to create them with git format-patch
All patches in here are DRBD specific, some might be gcc specific

TODO: transport_tcp: call windrbd_update_sizes()

Done (but maybe revert): drbd_main.c and others: locking primitives must be initialized by calling a function.
	Therefore change DEFINE_SPINLOCK to spinlock_t, write an initializer and call it in drbd_init. This already has been done. Review it.
	Update: if initializing to all zeros we can have the macro
	and save lots of DRBD patches. Check ReactOS source code
	for initialation code.

Done: drbd_main.c: export drbd_open (and try_to_promote also maybe)
	DRBD open is called via ops. try_to_promote is made non-static

Rejected: drbd_main.c: have a drbd_alloc_big_page_chain function
	And call it from drbd_transport_tcp.c. Do not change the
	signature of drbd_alloc_page_chain()

Rejected: GNU extension: drbd_int.h: Patch out __acquire in ({ ... }) macro

Rejected: GNU extension: drbd_receiver.c: initializer for union drbd_state cm and lo

Rejected: GNU extension: drbd_int.h: add type (struct resource, ...) to for_each_resource(...) macro definitions

Rejected: GNU extension: drbd_nl.c: str_to_info macro: replace ({ .. }) by ( .. )

Done: Various files: inter-function IRQ flags
	This is very hairy ...

! TODO: drbd_transport_tcp.c: setting SO_REUSEADDR by calling kernel_setsockopt
	This is a upstream canidate.
	In general accessing tcp internal data structures directly is
	probably not a good idea.
	There are 3 places in the source code.

Done: drbd_state.c (and drbd_int.h): wrcu_flags patch - replace by RCU flags passed between functions

Rejected: drbd_state.h: stable_state_change macro definition
	Needed?
	I don't think so.

Rejected: drbd_main.c: Have 'pages' of any size. ("big pages patch")

! Done: drbd_receiver.c: Under Windows, queriing a block device's size must happen at IRQL < DISPATCH_LEVEL
	Is it really needed?

Rejected: MSVC specific: drbd-headers/drbd_protocol.h: pragma pack(push, 1) (and pop)

Rejected: GNU extension: drbd_transport.h: tr_printk macros

Rejected: GNU extension: drbd_state.c: FINAL_STATE_CHANGE and REMEMBER_STATE_CHANGE macros.

TODO, maybe Reject: drbd_receiver.c: For each backing device wait for requests to complete
	in conn_disconnect()
	This solved a BSOD that was hard to track.
	But isn't that fixed with a wait_event() bugfix?
	Hmm .. I would prefer if we don't have this.

Rejected: GNU extension: drbd_transport.h: set_page_chain_next_offset_size uses gcc struct initializer

Rejected: GNU extension: page_chain_for_each macro uses ({ ... }).
	To optimize CPU cache ...

Done: drbd_transport_tcp.c: Windows does not support SOCK_STREAM before Windows Server 2019 ...

Rejected: MSVC extension: drbd_meta_data.h: __declspec(align(4096))

Done: drbd_state.h: state_change_lock prototypes: change flag parameter to KIRQL

Done: drbd_state.c: the change here is a %lu to a %llu it matters for volumes > 4TB

! TODO: drbd_main.c and others: use put_page() instead of free_page
	WinDRBD might hold the pages a little bit longer
	Hmm .. do we need that?
	I think yes!

Rejected: drbd_transport.h: make sure indices of pages are (at least) int, not short
	Hmm .. do we need that?
	No now that pages are PAGE_SIZE again.

Rejected: GNU extension: drbd_state.c: Change rv = stable_state_change(a, b, ...) to stable_state_change(rv, a, b, ...)
	Also return stable_state_change() - need an int tmp variable

Rejected: corking / uncorking of meta data I/O
	This maybe also makes the big pages patch unnecessary.
	Have a daemon that corks/uncorks instead. We shouldn't
	modify the backing device I/O code of DRBD for this
	(as it caused troubles in the field already).

Done: UL -> ULL at certain places
	We don't use cocci for that most of them are inside a
	ifdef BITS_PER_LONG == 64 ... (which should be 32 but
	is 64)

